==Battleground==
*3 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*12 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*2 [[Mr. Puffington]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Dealing with Puffington is simple on paper but the Haniwanwan swarm could be a handful unless promptly removed, as they will typically block Idi from hitting him. If that wasn't enough, two of him spawn over the course of the stage, and a Galactic Overseer Nyandam stays in the back, nuking anything walking into his range. The proper approach is to survive the onslaught by picking off the Haniwanwans before they accumulate, then kill off the remaining threats with whatever means necessary.

Alternatively:

Research Lv.50 [[Royal Guard Cat]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks]] - An excellent generalist midranger, Slapsticks are Strong Against Relics, with Curse Immunity. A stack of them will whittle Haniwanwans and can also evade Puffington's 300 range Omni Strike (350). Their slow speed makes them less likely to wander inside Galactic Overseer Nyandam's range, and they can be replaced fairly easily when lost. With talents, they can even weaken the Relics and extend the lifespan of other units.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] - Doron's 6.67-second Anti-Relic freeze and level 3 surge can paralyze Puffington, Loris, and groups of Haniwanwans thanks to his 600 range Omni Strike, giving other units an opportunity to burst them down before they cause too much trouble. Depending on the Surge spawn, he can even keep Puffington away for a while and chip Nyandam.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] - Can Can works best as a supplementary attacker here to land an occasional hit, as the Haniwanwans' sheer weight of fire and Puffington's attacks can overwhelm its slow, single target attacks easily. Its low cost does help here, as there are no reliable sources of funding and the Haniwanwans don't drop much to begin with.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Naala]] - Even before [[Atonement for Sin]], Naala still has the stats to take on the Relics here through its expansive LD reach that covers up to 700 range, as it is Strong Against Relics and Immune to Curse. While the weaken effect is inconsistent, Haniwanwan's Mini-Waves cannot hit it, and they can also keep this unit away from Nyandam's reach.
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]] - With Relic Talents (Curse Immunity, Target Relic), Gravolodon is able to near solo this stage with support from [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] and a couple meatshields, as he is able to tank both the Galactic Overseer Nyandam and Relics, not to mention his [[Immune to Waves|wave immunity]], which keeps him protected from the waves the Haniwanwans produce.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] - Being Immune to Waves with Massive Damage to Aliens/Relics, Royal Guard gets to optimize its short range here and can accumulate lots of DPS on all threats here. With a large research combo, Royal Guard even solo this stage.

==Trivia==
*Outta This Village's Japanese name, Ora Konna Kokyō Deruda ("I'm Leaving My Hometown"), is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Yoshi Ikuzō|Yoshi Ikuzō]] song "[[wikipedia:Ora Tōkyō sa Iguda|Ora Tōkyō sa Iguda]]" ("I'm Going to Tokyo"), in which the singer declares that he will leave his small hometown in the countryside to move to Tokyo.

